<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <record id="view_sapian_filing_list" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">sapian.filing.list</field>
        <field name="model">sapian.filing</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <list editable="bottom">
                <field name="filing_key"/>
                <field name="period_start"/>
                <field name="period_end"/>
                <field name="filed_on"/>
                <field name="reference"/>
                <field name="filed_by_id" optional="hide"/>
                <field name="company_id" groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
            </list>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="action_sapian_filing" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Filings Submitted</field>
        <field name="res_model">sapian.filing</field>
        <field name="view_mode">list</field>
        <field name="help" type="html">
            <p class="o_view_nocontent_smiling_face">Record a return once it has gone in</p>
            <p>Nothing else in SapianERP knows that a declaration was submitted —
            a posted payroll run is not a filing, and a printed VAT declaration is
            not one either. Recording it here is what turns "late" into "filed"
            on the overview.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="view_sapian_filing_deadline_list" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">sapian.filing.deadline.list</field>
        <field name="model">sapian.filing.deadline</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <list editable="bottom">
                <field name="filing_key"/>
                <field name="effective_from"/>
                <field name="deadline_window"/>
                <!-- Only read for the day-count shape, so it is hidden for the
                     other one rather than showing a 0 somebody would take for
                     "due the same day". -->
                <field name="days_after_period_end"
                       column_invisible="False"
                       invisible="deadline_window != 'days'"/>
                <field name="source_note"/>
                <field name="company_id" groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
            </list>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="action_sapian_filing_deadline" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Filing Deadlines</field>
        <field name="res_model">sapian.filing.deadline</field>
        <field name="view_mode">list</field>
        <field name="help" type="html">
            <p class="o_view_nocontent_smiling_face">When each return is due</p>
            <p>Effective-dated on purpose: correcting a deadline must never move a
            period that was already assessed against the old rule. Employment
            income tax is VERIFIED — it is due at the end of the following
            Ethiopian month. The other three keep a 30-day window that is
            UNVERIFIED against a current Ministry of Revenues schedule; each row
            carries the question that would settle it. Correct them here rather
            than in code.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="view_sapian_filing_period_list" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">sapian.filing.period.list</field>
        <field name="model">sapian.filing.period</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <list editable="bottom">
                <field name="filing_key"/>
                <field name="effective_from"/>
                <field name="calendar"/>
                <field name="source_note"/>
                <field name="company_id" groups="base.group_multi_company"/>
            </list>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="action_sapian_filing_period" model="ir.actions.act_window">
        <field name="name">Filing Periods</field>
        <field name="res_model">sapian.filing.period</field>
        <field name="view_mode">list</field>
        <field name="help" type="html">
            <p class="o_view_nocontent_smiling_face">Which calendar each return is counted in</p>
            <p>Employment income tax is filed for an ETHIOPIAN month — verified with
            two accountants and PwC. Whether VAT, withholding and pension are too is
            an open question, and until somebody answers it these rows record what
            the product does today rather than an answer. The note on each row is
            the exact question that would settle it. Answer one, change the row
            here, and every figure and deadline on the overview follows.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

</odoo>
